Subject: [PATCH 07196/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-15: root-cause the
 5699-14 lead -- trusted engine's search exhausts node budget, not a missing
 goal predicate

Added an optional diagnostics kwarg to plan_in_model() (arc_executable_world_model.py,
purely additive -- diagnostics=None is byte-identical to before) recording
is_level_complete_was_none/nodes_expanded/termination_reason on every return path.
Threaded through _call_plan_in_model's two production induction-tier call sites in
arc_competition_agent.py (mirrors the existing _planner_accepts_goal_energy pattern),
so the diagnostics flow into policy.induction_attempts -- already captured by
arc_sge_live_path_ab.py since REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-14, no script changes needed.

Re-ran sp80, budget=250 (same config as 5699-12/14). Answer: for the tier-1
CNN-dynamics-prior engine that passes its own held-out trust gate,
is_level_complete_was_none=false and termination_reason="max_nodes_reached" at
nodes_expanded ~20000 for BOTH arms independently (baseline: 20008, sge: 20002 --
near-identical counts from two separately-induced priors is a reproducibility
signal, not noise). Rules out both hypotheses REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-14 raised: not a
missing/broken goal predicate, not a fully-enumerated-empty search space. The
search genuinely runs out of its 20000-node budget without reaching the induced
goal predicate -- a search-budget-vs-compounding-model-error limit distinct from
exploration exhaustion (5699-13, ruled out) or router choice (5699-12, ruled out).
n=1 game/attempt -- a precisely root-caused lead, not a generalized capability
claim, per Sample-Size Rigor discipline.

